       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum adult dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you aren't a clinician, so this order needs a licensed prescriber to review it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe regimen now.** Examples are 400 mg four times daily, or 800 mg three times daily. Tell me which one.\n- **Hold the order for a prescriber.** The treating clinician can review it and place or confirm the dose they intend. If the clinician really wants a dose this high, they should document the reason through the hospital's override process with pharmacy involvement.\n\nWhich would you like?"
